  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1031 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nThis is a persistence forecast like no other; what you see is \nwhat you get for at least the next 7 days. With ongoing drought \nand no rain in sight, dry fuels and dry air have our guard up for \nfire danger for the rest of this week and maybe even into the \nweekend. The midlevel ridge over the eastern CONUS will persist \nfor the foreseeable future, resulting in mild days and cool nights\nwith less than 5% chance of rain. Again, lovely for most people \nbut comes as a double-edged sword with a risk of fire danger. Any \nfires that start will have a much easier time spreading under \nthese conditions. Drought WILL continue to worsen across the state\nand fire danger will likely increase the longer we go without \nrain.",
